From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xorbidden <xorbidden@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:54:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] userland/build.sh: stage fw-wifi/network for any radio

The network to join was installed into the small image only inside the
block that stages the WCN6750's firmware (wpss.mdt), so a phone with
another radio, whose firmware comes from elsewhere (the Mi 9T's WCN3990
runs its firmware on the modem), never got it and could not join with
wifi_station=1. Stage it on its own; SHARE=1 still leaves it out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 userland/build.sh | 13 ++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/userland/build.sh b/userland/build.sh
index b8d55eb..0bdc038 100755
--- a/userland/build.sh
+++ b/userland/build.sh
@@ -402,11 +402,14 @@ if [ -f ../fw-wifi/wpss.mdt ]; then
 	for f in bd_m20gl.elf regdb_xiaomi.bin; do
 		[ -f ../fw-wifi/qca6750/$f ] && install -m 0644 ../fw-wifi/qca6750/$f root/fw/
 	done
-	# the network the radio is to join: its name on the first line, its passphrase on the second. Yours, and
-	# so not in the repository; it goes where the firmware goes and the kernel reads it there (wifi_join=1)
-	rm -f root/fw/network
-	# SHARE=1: leave it out, for an image that is going to somebody else -- it is a passphrase
-	if [ -z "$SHARE" ] && [ -f ../fw-wifi/network ]; then install -m 0600 ../fw-wifi/network root/fw/network; fi
+fi
+# the network the radio is to join, whatever the radio: its name on the first line, its passphrase on the second.
+# Yours, and so not in the repository; it goes where the firmware goes and the kernel reads it there (wifi_join=1,
+# wifi_station=1). SHARE=1: leave it out, for an image that is going to somebody else -- it is a passphrase
+rm -f root/fw/network
+if [ -z "$SHARE" ] && [ -f ../fw-wifi/network ]; then
+	mkdir -p root/fw
+	install -m 0600 ../fw-wifi/network root/fw/network
 fi
 # ... and the vibration motor's waveforms, the phone's /vendor/firmware/aw8697_haptic.bin, from ../fw-haptic
 # (drivers/haptic/hakios.haptic.c, haptic=3; 3.6 KB, the vendor's and not in the repository either)
